The main issue was that we were trying to set up the window functions after the component started rendering, which was too late. By setting them up immediately when the module loads, we ensure they're available when the CalcomThemeProvider needs them.

This should resolve the "window.getEmbedTheme is not a function" error because now we're ensuring that:
1. The function exists before any React code runs
2. It's actually a function (not null)
3. It's properly typed with TypeScript
4. It's available globally on the window object

